<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>Module 103 — Unit 340 · Ammonia Refrigeration</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --crimson:#C8102E; --crimson-dark:#9E0C24; --ink:#15171A; --ink-soft:#4A4F57;
    --line:#E2E5E9; --line-strong:#C9CED4; --bg:#FFFFFF; --bg-soft:#F7F8FA; --ok:#1F8A4C;
    --amber:#B26A00; --blue:#0B5CAD;
    --sans:"Segoe UI","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif; --mono:"Consolas","SF Mono","Courier New",monospace;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  html,body{margin:0;height:100%;}
  body{font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--ink);background:#ECEEF1;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:100vh;padding:16px;}

  .deck{width:100%;max-width:1040px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:4px;box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.10);display:flex;flex-direction:column;
    height:min(720px,94vh);overflow:hidden;}

  .brandbar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;
    padding:13px 30px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);flex:none;}
  .brandbar .vendor img{height:48px;display:block;}
  .clients{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;}
  .clients .role{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--ink-soft);writing-mode:vertical-rl;transform:rotate(180deg);}
  .client-logos{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;}
  .client-logo{height:35px;width:auto;display:block;}
  .client-logo.itf{height:39px;}
  .client-logos .divider{width:1px;height:32px;background:var(--line-strong);}
  .accent{height:3px;background:var(--crimson);flex:none;}
  body.fsmode{padding:0;background:#000;}
  body.fsmode .deck{border:none;border-radius:0;box-shadow:none;}
  .nav.on{background:var(--ink);color:#fff;border-color:var(--ink);}

  .stage{position:relative;flex:1;overflow:hidden;}
  .slide{position:absolute;inset:0;padding:30px 44px;overflow:auto;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transition:opacity .22s ease;}
  .slide.active{opacity:1;visibility:visible;}
  .pres{position:absolute;top:16px;right:28px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:4px 11px;border-radius:20px;border:1.5px solid;z-index:4;}
  .pres.mm{color:var(--crimson);border-color:var(--crimson);background:#FBE9EC;}
  .pres.zr{color:var(--blue);border-color:var(--blue);background:#EAF3FB;}
  .pres.lz{color:var(--ok);border-color:var(--ok);background:#E7F5EC;}
  .cover3d .pres.mm{color:#fff;border-color:#ff6478;background:rgba(200,16,46,.55);}
  .kicker{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:9px;}
  .kicker .sub{color:var(--ink-soft);font-weight:400;}
  h1{font-size:29px;margin:0 0 6px;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.1;}
  h2{font-size:24px;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.15;}
  p.lead{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.58;max-width:72ch;margin:0 0 13px;}
  ul.points{margin:5px 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;}
  ul.points li{position:relative;padding:6px 0 6px 21px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);}
  ul.points li:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:2px;top:13px;width:7px;height:7px;background:var(--crimson);border-radius:1px;}
  ul.points li b{color:var(--ink);}
  .muted{color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:13px 24px;}

  table.data{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px;margin-top:3px;}
  table.data th{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--ink-soft);text-align:left;padding:7px 9px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line-strong);}
  table.data td{padding:7px 9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;}
  table.data td.k{font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;}
  table.data td.v{color:var(--ink-soft);}

  .facts{display:flex;gap:13px;margin-top:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .fact{flex:1;min-width:140px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:13px 15px;background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .fact .n{font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);font-family:var(--mono);line-height:1;}
  .fact .l{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:6px;line-height:1.35;}
  .slide.cover3d{display:flex;flex-direction:column;color:#fff;
    background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(11,13,15,.80),rgba(11,13,15,.55) 45%,rgba(11,13,15,.82)),url('/images/3D_330-bw.png') center/cover no-repeat;}
  .slide.cover3d h1{color:#fff;}
  .slide.cover3d .kicker{color:#ff6478;}
  .slide.cover3d .kicker .sub{color:#c9ccd1;}
  .slide.cover3d .lead{color:#e4e6ea;max-width:60ch;}
  .slide.cover3d .params{margin-top:auto;}
  .slide.cover3d .fact{background:rgba(255,255,255,.10);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.24);}
  .slide.cover3d .fact .n{color:#fff;font-size:20px;}
  .slide.cover3d .fact .l{color:#c7cad0;}
  .slide.cover3d .owner{margin-top:12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#aeb2b8;}
  .slide.cover3d .owner b{color:#fff;}

  .flow{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;margin-top:4px;}
  .step{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--crimson);
    border-radius:4px;padding:8px 12px;background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .step .u{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:700;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--crimson);min-width:74px;}
  .step .t{font-size:13px;}
  .step .t b{color:var(--ink);}

  /* slide 05 — la franja de U530 pide 170 px que la slide no tenía. No se
     recorta contenido para hacerle sitio: se aprieta el interlineado de la
     lista y de la tabla de horarios, que iban holgadas. La regla queda ACOTADA
     a esta slide para no cambiar el ritmo de las otras 27. */
  .slide.m101scope ul.points li{font-size:13.2px;padding:5px 0 5px 19px;line-height:1.4;}
  .slide.m101scope ul.points li:before{top:12px;}
  .slide.m101scope table.timeline td{padding-top:2.5px;padding-bottom:2.5px;font-size:12px;}
  .slide.m101scope .lead{font-size:13.5px;}
  .slide.m101scope table.timeline td.seg{line-height:1.3;}
  /* fichas de equipo (12a..12d) · la regla global .eqdetail reserva 58 px para el
     encabezado, medida sobre la lamina antigua. Estas cuatro se pasaban 5 px y
     desbordaban las cuatro; se aprieta SOLO aqui, sin tocar la regla global. */
  .slide.m101ds .eqdetail{height:calc(100% - 66px);}
  .slide.m101ds h2{margin-bottom:11px;}
  /* láminas de instrumentación (22 · 23) · los dibujos crecieron al pasar a
     globos ISA con su leyenda; se aprieta lo que los rodea, no la regla global.
     La 23 lleva además una tabla de 7 lazos que es material de examen: se
     estrecha, no se quita. */
  .slide.m101inst .mapwrap{padding:5px 9px 3px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mapwrap + .mapwrap{margin-top:6px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mgrid{margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mgrid .objtile{padding:4px 3px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mgrid .objtile .n{font-size:17px;margin-top:3px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mgrid .objtile .ic{width:21px;height:21px;font-size:12px;}
  .slide.m101inst table.data{font-size:10.4px !important;margin-top:5px;}
  .slide.m101inst table.data td, .slide.m101inst table.data th{padding-top:2.5px;padding-bottom:2.5px;}
  .slide.m101inst .routing, .slide.m101inst .note{margin-top:5px;}
  .slide.m101inst .mgrid{margin-top:6px;}
  /* botonera de planos — slide 08. Regla global (no acotada): cualquier lámina que
     tenga un plano detrás puede usarla, que es justo lo que evita reinventarla. */
  /* align-items:stretch para que el botón del PFD, que no lleva subtítulo, quede a la
     misma altura que los dos que sí lo llevan. */
  .docbtns{display:flex;align-items:stretch;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:-4px 0 10px;}
  .docbtn{display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:1px;text-decoration:none;
    border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-left:3px solid var(--crimson);border-radius:7px;
    background:#fff;padding:5px 12px 6px;transition:.15s;}
  .docbtn b{font-size:12px;color:var(--crimson);line-height:1.2;}
  .docbtn b:after{content:" ↗";font-weight:400;}
  .docbtn span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.2;}
  .docbtn:hover{background:#FBE9EC;border-color:var(--crimson);}
  .docbtn.gone{border-left-color:var(--line-strong);pointer-events:none;opacity:.55;}
  .docbtn.gone b{color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .docbtn.gone b:after{content:" · file missing";font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;font-weight:400;}
  /* slide 08 · reproductor de vídeo. La slide es `position:absolute; inset:0`, así que
     con flex-column el .vidbox se come todo el alto que sobre de la cabecera; el <video>
     lleva object-fit:contain para no deformar el material de origen. Todo acotado a
     .m101video: ninguna otra slide usa flex a nivel de sección. */
  .slide.m101video{display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:18px 26px 16px;overflow:hidden;}
  .slide.m101video.active{display:flex;}
  .slide.m101video .vidhd{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;flex:0 0 auto;}
  .slide.m101video .vidhd h2{margin:0;font-size:21px;}
  .slide.m101video .vidhd .kicker{margin-bottom:5px;}
  .slide.m101video .vidtabs{display:flex;gap:8px;flex:0 0 auto;}
  .slide.m101video .vidtabs button{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;cursor:pointer;
    border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-top:3px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:9px;
    background:#fff;padding:7px 14px;font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-soft);
    transition:.15s;}
  .slide.m101video .vidtabs button:hover{border-color:var(--crimson);color:var(--ink);}
  .slide.m101video .vidtabs button.on{border-color:var(--crimson);border-top-color:var(--crimson);color:var(--ink);background:#FBE9EC;}
  .slide.m101video .vidtabs button .dur{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;
    color:var(--crimson);background:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:2px 8px;}
  .slide.m101video .vidbox{flex:1 1 auto;min-height:0;margin-top:11px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius:10px;background:#0e0f11;overflow:hidden;position:relative;}
  .slide.m101video .vidbox video{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;object-fit:contain;background:#0e0f11;}
  .slide.m101video .vidmiss{position:absolute;inset:0;display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    text-align:center;color:#c9ced6;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;padding:26px;}
  .slide.m101video .vidbox.missing .vidmiss{display:flex;}
  .slide.m101video .vidfoot{flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  /* slide de documentos (hoy la 20) · el registro pasó de 9 a 15 filas (migración 195):
     se aprieta
     sólo esta slide, sin tocar la regla global de .data que usan las otras 27. */
  .slide.m101docs table.data td, .slide.m101docs table.data th{padding-top:3.5px;padding-bottom:3.5px;line-height:1.25;}
  .slide.m101docs table.data{font-size:11px !important;}
  .slide.m101docs .note{margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.m101scope table.timeline .tp{display:block;font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);font-weight:400;margin-top:1px;line-height:1.32;}
  .slide.m101scope .note{margin-top:8px;padding-top:6px;}
  .note{margin-top:14px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);border-top:1px dashed var(--line-strong);padding-top:9px;line-height:1.5;}
  .fig{margin-top:8px;text-align:center;}
  .fig a{display:inline-block;text-decoration:none;}
  .fig img{max-width:100%;max-height:320px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:5px;background:#fff;cursor:zoom-in;}
  .fig .cap{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:6px;letter-spacing:.04em;}
  .figrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr;gap:18px;align-items:center;}
  .figrow ul.points li{font-size:13px;}
  .team{display:flex;gap:18px;margin-top:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .person{flex:1;min-width:220px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;padding:18px 20px;background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .person .av{width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--crimson);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px;font-family:var(--mono);}
  .person .av.zr{background:var(--blue);}
  .person .av.gn{background:var(--ok);}
  .person .rl.gn{color:var(--ok);}
  .person .nm{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;}
  .person .rl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--crimson);margin-top:3px;}
  .person .rl.zr{color:var(--blue);}
  .person .org{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:6px;}
  .zagenda{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;margin-top:12px;}
  .zag{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;}
  .zag .n{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:#2b2e33;color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;flex:none;}
  .zag.red .n{background:var(--crimson);}
  .zag b{display:block;font-size:15.5px;}
  .zag span{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .carousel{position:relative;height:322px;margin-top:8px;}
  .carousel .cimg{position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;opacity:0;transition:opacity .55s;pointer-events:none;}
  .carousel .cimg.active{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto;}
  .carousel .cimg img{max-width:100%;max-height:300px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:5px;background:#fff;cursor:zoom-in;}
  .carousel .cdots{position:absolute;bottom:2px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:8px;z-index:3;}
  .carousel .cdots b{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:#c9ced4;cursor:pointer;display:block;}
  .carousel .cdots b.active{background:var(--crimson);}
  .carousel .ccap{position:absolute;bottom:14px;left:0;right:0;text-align:center;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);letter-spacing:.04em;pointer-events:none;}
  .btn-doc{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;background:#fff;color:var(--crimson);border:1.5px solid var(--crimson);
    text-decoration:none;padding:7px 13px;border-radius:5px;font-weight:600;font-size:12.5px;}
  .btn-doc:hover{background:var(--crimson);color:#fff;}

  .timeline{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px;margin-top:4px;}
  .timeline td{padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);}
  .timeline td.seg{font-weight:600;}
  .timeline td.dur,.timeline td.cum{font-family:var(--mono);white-space:nowrap;}
  .timeline td.cum{color:var(--ink-soft);text-align:right;}
  .timeline tr.brk td{background:#FFF7EC;color:var(--amber);}
  .timeline tr.tot td{border-top:2px solid var(--line-strong);font-weight:700;}

  .inter{height:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;}
  .inter .big{font-size:54px;font-weight:700;font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--crimson);line-height:1;}
  .inter h2{font-size:30px;margin:14px 0 6px;}
  .inter p{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:15px;max-width:50ch;}
  .inter.brk .big{color:var(--amber);}

  .navbar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px;padding:10px 22px;
    border-top:1px solid var(--line);flex:none;background:#fff;}
  .counter{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-soft);letter-spacing:.05em;}
  .navmid{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;}
  .navbtns{display:flex;gap:7px;}
  button.nav{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:#fff;color:var(--ink);font-size:13px;font-weight:600;
    padding:7px 14px;border-radius:4px;cursor:pointer;transition:.12s;}
  button.nav:hover:not(:disabled){border-color:var(--crimson);color:var(--crimson);}
  button.nav:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:not-allowed;}
  button.nav.primary{background:var(--crimson);color:#fff;border-color:var(--crimson);}
  button.nav.primary:hover{background:var(--crimson-dark);}
  .progress{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;height:2px;background:var(--line);}
  .progress > i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--crimson);transition:width .22s;}

  @media (max-width:700px){
    .slide{padding:22px 20px;} h1{font-size:22px;} h2{font-size:19px;}
    .grid2{grid-template-columns:1fr;} .brandbar{padding:11px 16px;}
  }

  /* ===== Area-introduction components (map+HMB · physical) ===== */

  /* ═══ slides 10-22 · equipment-detail band + the LOC330 locator ═══════════════
     Three .loc rules are the locator contract (highlight by data attribute, never
     by editing geometry). The .eqd330 block is a compact modifier scoped to these
     13 slides only: it buys ~55 px so locator + 4 cards fit the 587 px stage.
     Do not widen it to the global rules. */
  .loc svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;color:var(--ink);}
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq]{opacity:.30;transition:opacity .2s ease,color .2s ease;}
  /* the highlighted machine is DRAWN IN RED, the way the old stage slides did it: the
     P&ID symbols inherit `color` and stroke with currentColor, so setting color on the .on
     group turns its whole geometry crimson, and the text rule takes tag + sub-labels. */
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].on{opacity:1;color:var(--crimson);}
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].on text{fill:var(--crimson);}
  /* BOX style (.eqb, gas sheet / slides 10-12): the fill IS the highlight, so box groups
     are never dimmed - white box + grey border by default, solid crimson + white text when
     .on. Same language as the old Module-101 stage slides. */
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].eqb{opacity:1;}
  .loc [data-eq].eqb .eqbox{fill:#fff;stroke:var(--line-strong);}
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].eqb.on .eqbox{fill:var(--crimson);stroke:var(--crimson);}
  .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].eqb.on text{fill:#fff;}
  .slide.eqd330{padding:23px 44px 13px;}
  .slide.eqd330 h2{margin-bottom:10px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .kicker{margin-bottom:7px;}
  .slide.eqd330 ul.points{margin-top:0;}
  .slide.eqd330 ul.points li{font-size:12.4px;line-height:1.33;padding:3.6px 0 3.6px 18px;}
  .slide.eqd330 ul.points li:before{top:10px;width:6px;height:6px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .ctlwrap,.slide.eqd330 .almwrap{margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .hcard .hh{font-size:8.8px;padding:3.5px 9px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .hcard .hb{padding:4px 9px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .hval{font-size:10.4px;padding:1.3px 0;line-height:1.26;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqcard .hd{padding:5px 11px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqcard .hd .tag{font-size:15px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqcard .hd .ty{font-size:9.2px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqcard .bd{padding:4px 11px;overflow:visible;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqspecs{gap:0 14px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqspecs .er .k{white-space:nowrap;flex:0 0 auto;}
  .slide.eqd330 .eqspecs .er{font-size:10.2px;padding:1.3px 0;line-height:1.24;}
  .slide.eqd330 .grid2{gap:10px 20px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .collbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;padding:0 0 3px 2px;}
  /* slide 12 only · the loop-sequence strip under the three pills */
  .slide.eqd330 .seqwrap{margin-top:11px;padding:7px 12px 6px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .loopseq{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:0 4px;padding:4px 0 1px;}
  .slide.eqd330 .loopseq span{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex:1 1 0;min-width:0;}
  .slide.eqd330 .loopseq b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);white-space:nowrap;}
  .slide.eqd330 .loopseq em{font-style:normal;font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:2px;white-space:nowrap;}
  .slide.eqd330 .loopseq span+span{border-left:1px solid var(--line);}

  /* ═══ slides 13-19 · the SAME amineblock sheet slide 11 uses ════════════════
     Mario, 2026-07-30: reuse the finished loop drawing on every amine-loop
     machine, in slide 11's band exactly -- caption + descriptions on the left,
     control elements and alarms on the right. The equipment (specs) card was
     removed on Mario's instruction, which is what pays for the taller sheet:
     these slides render it at FULL width, like slide 11. The spec figures are
     in each slide's data-notes, not lost. Do not reintroduce the specs card
     here without re-measuring -- it is what forced the sheet to 84 % before. */
  .slide.amb330 .grid2>div>.ctlwrap:first-child{margin-top:0;}
  /* amineblock is a BOX sheet: crimson IS the highlight, so nothing dims here --
     not even the three pump symbols, or they ghost while the boxes stay solid. */
  .slide.amb330 .loc[data-hi] [data-eq]{opacity:1;}
  .slide.amb330 .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].on{color:var(--crimson);}

  .mapwrap{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--bg-soft);padding:7px 10px 3px;}
  .mapwrap .lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);padding:0 2px 2px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;}
  .mapwrap .lbl .you{color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;}
  .hmb{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-top:11px;align-items:stretch;}
  .hcard{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;position:relative;}
  .hcard .hh{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#fff;padding:5px 10px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;}
  .hcard.in .hh{background:var(--blue);}
  .hcard.mid .hh{background:var(--amber);}
  .hcard.out .hh{background:var(--ok);}
  .hcard .hb{padding:7px 10px;}
  .hval{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;font-size:11.5px;padding:2.5px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);line-height:1.3;}
  .hval:last-child{border-bottom:none;}
  .hval .k{color:var(--ink-soft);} .hval .v{font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;text-align:right;}
  .hstrip{display:flex;gap:9px;margin-top:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .pill{flex:1;min-width:190px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;background:var(--bg-soft);padding:7px 12px;font-size:11px;line-height:1.4;}
  .pill b{color:var(--crimson);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:2px;}
  .pill .big{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);}
  .routing{margin-top:8px;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);border-top:1px dashed var(--line-strong);padding-top:6px;}
  .routing b{color:var(--ink);}
  .p2cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-top:11px;}
  .hcard.arloc .hh{background:#2b2e33;} .hcard.eqc .hh{background:var(--crimson);}
  .hcard.ioc .hh{background:var(--blue);} .hcard.enc .hh{background:var(--amber);}
  .hcard.iso .hh{background:#C8102E;} .hcard.bdw .hh{background:#B26A00;}
  .hcard.rel .hh{background:#7A3FB3;} .hcard.ctl .hh{background:#0B5CAD;}
  .vgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-top:10px;}
  .mgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:8px;margin-top:10px;}
  .doclink{color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;}
  .doclink:hover{text-decoration:underline;}
  .docstat{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;font-weight:700;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:10px;letter-spacing:.04em;}
  .docstat.on{background:#E7F5EC;color:#1F8A4C;} .docstat.off{background:#F0F1F3;color:#8a9099;}
  .doccat{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .carea{position:relative;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);}
  .carea .cimg{position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;opacity:0;transition:opacity .8s ease;pointer-events:none;}
  .carea .cimg.on{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto;}
  .carea .cimg img{max-width:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:contain;}
  .carea .cbadge{position:absolute;top:11px;left:12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff;background:rgba(200,16,46,.85);padding:4px 10px;border-radius:20px;}
  .carea .cdots{position:absolute;bottom:10px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:7px;z-index:3;}
  .carea .cdots b{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(0,0,0,.22);cursor:pointer;display:block;transition:.12s;}
  .carea .cdots b.on{background:var(--crimson);transform:scale(1.15);}
  /* equipment datasheet */
  .eqdetail{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1.15fr;gap:14px;height:calc(100% - 58px);}
  .eqfig{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;background:#fff;padding:6px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0;}
  .eqfig .imgbox{position:relative;flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden;min-height:0;}
  .eqfig img{max-width:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:contain;border-radius:4px;}
  .eqfig .eqc-img{position:absolute;inset:0;margin:auto;opacity:0;transition:opacity .5s;pointer-events:none;}
  .eqfig .eqc-img.on{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto;}
  .eqfig .eqc-count{position:absolute;top:6px;right:8px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-soft);background:rgba(255,255,255,.85);padding:2px 7px;border-radius:10px;z-index:3;}
  .eqfig .eqc-dots{position:absolute;bottom:5px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:6px;z-index:3;}
  .eqfig .eqc-dots b{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(0,0,0,.22);cursor:pointer;display:block;}
  .eqfig .eqc-dots b.on{background:var(--crimson);}
  .eqfig .cap{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);text-align:center;padding:6px 4px 2px;flex:none;}
  .stage img{cursor:zoom-in;}
  .eqcol{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0;}
  .eqcard{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0;flex:1;}
  .eqcard .hd{background:var(--crimson);color:#fff;padding:8px 13px;flex:none;}
  .eqcard .hd .tag{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:19px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;}
  .eqcard .hd .ty{font-size:10.5px;opacity:.92;margin-top:2px;}
  .eqcard .bd{padding:7px 13px;overflow:auto;}
  .eqspecs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0 16px;}
  .eqspecs .er{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;font-size:11px;padding:3px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);line-height:1.3;}
  .eqspecs .er .k{color:var(--ink-soft);} .eqspecs .er .v{font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;text-align:right;}
  .eqthumbs{display:flex;gap:6px;margin-top:9px;flex:none;}
  .eqthumbs button{flex:1;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;font-weight:700;border:1.5px solid var(--line-strong);background:#fff;color:var(--ink-soft);border-radius:6px;padding:6px 3px;cursor:pointer;transition:.12s;}
  .eqthumbs button:hover{border-color:var(--crimson);color:var(--crimson);}
  .eqthumbs button.on{background:var(--crimson);border-color:var(--crimson);color:#fff;}
  /* technological-objects tiles + details modal */
  .objgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(9,1fr);gap:7px;margin-top:11px;}
  .objtile{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-top:3px solid var(--acc,#C8102E);border-radius:10px;background:#fff;
    padding:10px 6px;text-align:center;cursor:pointer;transition:.14s;font-family:inherit;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;}
  .objtile:hover{border-color:var(--acc,#C8102E);box-shadow:0 5px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.10);transform:translateY(-2px);}
  .objtile .ic{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:9px;background:var(--bg-soft);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:17px;color:var(--acc,#C8102E);}
  .objtile .n{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:var(--acc,#C8102E);line-height:1;margin-top:7px;}
  .objtile .l{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);margin-top:3px;line-height:1.2;}
  /* discipline band — same cards, icons and grouping as eni/index.html (fact + discBand).
     Four boxes of equal width; the cards inside sit on a 2-column grid so every
     card is the same size no matter how many a discipline carries. */
  .dband{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1.2fr 1.2fr 1.1fr;gap:8px;margin-top:9px;align-items:stretch;}
  /* a discipline drawn as a square (tam-disc) — the SVG carries its own frame */
  .dsq{min-width:0;}
  .dsq svg{display:block;width:100%;}
  .dsqfoot{margin-top:5px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.2px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.03em;
    color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.35;cursor:pointer;}
  .dsqfoot i{font-style:normal;font-weight:400;}
  .dsqfoot:hover{color:var(--crimson);}
  .dbox{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:9px;
    padding:7px 8px 8px;background:linear-gradient(#FFFFFF,#F7F9FB);}
  .dbox .dhd{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:6px;margin:0 0 6px 1px;}
  .dbox .dt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;padding-top:3px;}
  .dbox .dtot{margin-left:auto;text-align:right;line-height:1;}
  .dbox .dtot b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);}
  .dbox .dtot span{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:7px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  /* every card is one row tall, sized for a TWO-LINE label, so a card with a
     short label and one with a wrapped label keep the same box. */
  .dfacts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:5px;align-content:start;grid-auto-rows:50px;}
  .dfacts.one{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);}
  .dfacts.three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));}
  /* three columns leave less room for the word: step the label down rather than clip it */
  .dfacts.three .dfact{grid-template-columns:20px minmax(0,1fr);gap:6px;padding:5px 6px;}
  .dfacts.three .dfact .ficon{width:20px;height:20px;}
  .dfacts.three .dfact .ficon svg{width:13px;height:13px;}
  .dfacts.three .dfact .l{font-size:6.2px;letter-spacing:.02em;}
  .dfact{display:grid;grid-template-columns:22px minmax(0,1fr);align-items:center;gap:7px;
    border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:#fff;padding:6px 8px;cursor:pointer;
    font-family:inherit;text-align:left;min-width:0;transition:transform .13s,box-shadow .13s,border-color .13s;}
  .dfact:hover{border-color:var(--crimson);box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.09);transform:translateY(-1px);}
  .dfact .ficon{width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:7px;background:rgba(200,16,46,.075);color:var(--crimson);
    display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;}
  .dfact .ficon svg{width:14px;height:14px;}
  .dfact .fbody{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;line-height:1;min-width:0;}
  .dfact .n{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);}
  .dfact .l{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:6.9px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.03em;color:var(--ink-soft);
    text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.25;max-width:100%;
    display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;}
  .objmodal{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(15,17,20,.55);display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:50;padding:24px;}
  .objmodal.on{display:flex;}
  .objbox{background:#fff;border-radius:12px;width:min(960px,95vw);max-height:88vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.35);}
  .objhd{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:13px 18px;background:var(--crimson);color:#fff;flex:none;}
  .objhd span{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;}
  .objhd button{background:rgba(255,255,255,.16);border:none;color:#fff;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;}
  .objtblwrap{overflow:auto;}
  .objtbl{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;}
  .objtbl th{position:sticky;top:0;background:#fff;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);text-align:left;padding:9px 14px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line-strong);}
  .objtbl td{padding:7px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top;}
  .objtbl td.tg{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);white-space:nowrap;}
  .objtbl td.ty{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .objtbl tr:hover td{background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .objempty{padding:26px 20px;text-align:center;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:13px;}
  .objfoot{flex:none;padding:8px 18px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-soft);border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
  /* cause & effect matrix */
  .cewrap{padding:14px 16px;}
  .cematrix{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;margin:0 auto;}
  .cematrix th,.cematrix td{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);padding:5px 8px;}
  .cematrix thead th{background:var(--bg-soft);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);vertical-align:bottom;}
  .cematrix th.eff{writing-mode:vertical-rl;transform:rotate(180deg);white-space:nowrap;height:104px;text-align:left;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.03em;}
  .cematrix td.tg{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);white-space:nowrap;}
  .cematrix td.ins{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .cematrix td.ds{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--ink);max-width:230px;}
  .cematrix td.mk{text-align:center;font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);font-size:15px;background:#FBE9EC;}
  .cematrix td.sp{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);white-space:nowrap;}
  .cebadge{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:10px;}
  .cebadge.psd{background:#FBE9EC;color:#C8102E;} .cebadge.lsd{background:#FFF3E0;color:#B26A00;}
  .celegend{margin-top:13px;font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.55;}
  .celegend b{color:var(--ink);} .celegend .cetag{font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;}
  .celegend .row{margin:2px 0;}
  /* interactive cause & effect (on-slide) */
  .cematrix tbody tr.hi td{background:#FBE9EC;}
  .cematrix thead th.effhi{background:#C8102E;color:#fff;}
  .cematrix td.mkhi{background:#C8102E;color:#fff;}
  .cematrix tbody tr,.cematrix thead th.eff{cursor:pointer;}
  .cematrix tbody tr.dim{opacity:.35;}
  .cehint{font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:8px;}
  .cehint b{color:var(--crimson);}
  /* global image lightbox */
  .lightbox{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(8,9,11,.92);display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    flex-direction:column;z-index:120;padding:26px;cursor:zoom-out;}
  .lightbox.on{display:flex;}
  .lightbox img{max-width:96vw;max-height:88vh;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 20px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.6);background:#fff;}
  .lightbox .lbcap{color:#e6e7e9;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;margin-top:12px;text-align:center;max-width:80vw;}
  .lightbox .lbclose{position:fixed;top:16px;right:20px;color:#fff;font-size:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.14);
    border:none;width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;}
  /* ═══ UNIT 530 · Block 3 ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Todo acotado a sus propias clases: ni una regla global tocada, para no
     cambiar el ritmo de las 31 slides que ya estaban (misma disciplina que
     .m101scope / .m101video). */
  .slide.u530cover .big{font-size:64px;letter-spacing:.02em;}
  .slide.u530cover h2{font-size:27px;margin:10px 0 5px;}
  .slide.u530cover p{font-size:14.5px;max-width:64ch;}
  .u530chain{display:flex;align-items:stretch;justify-content:center;gap:5px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0 4px;}
  .u530chain span{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:2px;min-width:104px;padding:9px 11px;
    border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-top:3px solid var(--crimson);border-radius:9px;background:#fff;}
  .u530chain span b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--crimson);}
  .u530chain span i{font-style:normal;font-size:9.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);letter-spacing:.04em;}
  .u530chain span.pond{border-top-color:var(--blue);}
  .u530chain span.pond b{color:var(--blue);font-size:11.5px;}
  .u530chain em{display:flex;align-items:center;font-style:normal;color:var(--line-strong);font-size:16px;}
  .u530sub{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft) !important;margin-top:14px !important;}
  /* rejilla de contadores: seis, no nueve como en U200 */
  .objgrid.u530grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);}
  /* un contador que no existe en la base no imprime un numero: imprime raya en ambar */
  .objtile.gap .n{color:var(--amber);}
  .objtile.gap{border-top-style:dashed;}
  .note .amb{color:var(--amber);}
  .note code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;background:var(--bg-soft);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;}
  table.data.u530io{font-size:11px;margin-top:0;}
  table.data.u530io th{padding:4px 8px;}
  table.data.u530io td{padding:4px 8px;line-height:1.3;}
  table.data.u530io td.tg{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);white-space:nowrap;width:1%;}
  table.data.u530io td.ty{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;color:var(--ink-soft);white-space:nowrap;}
  /* la slide de video de U530 reutiliza .m101video; solo cambia la cabecera,
     que aqui lleva la duracion en vez de las pestañas de dos ficheros */
  .slide.m101video .viddur{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--ink-soft);border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:5px 9px;flex:0 0 auto;}
  /* P&ID a pantalla completa con zoom. Mismo esqueleto flex que .m101video:
     cabecera fija, caja elastica, nota al pie. */
  .slide.m530pid{display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:18px 26px 16px;overflow:hidden;}
  .slide.m530pid.active{display:flex;}
  .slide.m530pid .vidhd{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;flex:0 0 auto;}
  .slide.m530pid .vidhd h2{margin:0;font-size:21px;}
  .slide.m530pid .vidhd .kicker{margin-bottom:5px;}
  .slide.m530pid .note{margin-top:7px;padding-top:7px;flex:0 0 auto;font-size:11px;}
  .pidctl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;flex:0 0 auto;}
  .pidctl button{width:28px;height:28px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:#fff;border-radius:6px;
    cursor:pointer;font-size:15px;line-height:1;color:var(--ink);}
  .pidctl button#p47fit{width:auto;padding:0 9px;font-size:11px;font-family:var(--mono);}
  .pidctl button:hover{border-color:var(--crimson);color:var(--crimson);}
  .pidctl #p47pct{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-soft);min-width:44px;text-align:center;}
  .pidctl a{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--crimson);text-decoration:none;margin-left:4px;}
  .pidbox{flex:1 1 auto;min-height:0;margin-top:11px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:10px;
    background:#fff;position:relative;overflow:hidden;cursor:grab;}
  .pidbox.drag{cursor:grabbing;}
  .pidbox img{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;transform-origin:0 0;image-rendering:auto;user-select:none;-webkit-user-drag:none;}
  .pidmiss{position:absolute;inset:0;display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;
    padding:26px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--amber);background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .pidbox.missing .pidmiss{display:flex;}
  .pidbox.missing img,.pidbox.missing .pidhint{display:none;}
  .pidhint{position:absolute;right:9px;bottom:8px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);background:rgba(255,255,255,.86);border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:5px;padding:3px 7px;pointer-events:none;}
  /* las dos slides densas de U530, acotadas: cabian en 1600x900 pero no en el
     alto real del .stage. Mismo patron que .m101scope / .m101inst. */
  .slide.u530area .carea{height:430px !important;}
  .slide.u530area .objgrid{margin-top:8px;}
  .slide.u530area .objtile{padding:6px 4px;}
  .slide.u530area .objtile .ic{width:24px;height:24px;font-size:13px;}
  .slide.u530area .objtile .n{font-size:20px;margin-top:5px;}
  .slide.u530area .note{margin-top:9px;padding-top:7px;}
  .slide.u530map .mapwrap{max-width:63%;margin:0 auto;padding:5px 9px 2px;}
  .slide.u530map h2{margin-bottom:8px;}
  .slide.u530map .grid2{margin-top:8px !important;}
  .slide.u530map table.data.u530io td, .slide.u530map table.data.u530io th{padding:2.5px 7px;}
  .slide.u530map table.data.u530io{font-size:10.2px;}
  .slide.u530map .note{margin-top:8px;padding-top:7px;font-size:10.5px;}
  /* algo que sólo existe al imprimir (el vídeo no se puede imprimir) */
  .printonly{display:none;}

  /* print / export-to-PDF: cada slide es una pagina, y el cromo (navbar, barra de
     progreso, lightbox, modales) desaparece. Mismo bloque que el modulo 002, mas
     los anadidos que pide este deck: las dos slides de video, la del P&ID con
     zoom, las fichas de equipo y el mapa acotado de U530. */
  @media print{
    *{-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;}
    @page{size:1040px 720px;margin:0;}
    html,body{background:#fff !important;display:block !important;min-height:0 !important;padding:0 !important;width:1040px;}
    .deck{width:1040px !important;max-width:none !important;height:auto !important;border:none !important;
      box-shadow:none !important;border-radius:0 !important;display:block !important;}
    .navbar,.progress,.lightbox,.objmodal{display:none !important;}
    .brandbar{position:fixed;top:0;left:0;width:1040px;background:#fff;z-index:5;}
    .accent{position:fixed;top:77px;left:0;width:1040px;z-index:5;}
    .stage{position:static !important;overflow:visible !important;height:auto !important;flex:none !important;}
    /* padding-top (y no un margen del .stage) para que el hueco de la cabecera
       fija se repita en TODAS las paginas impresas */
    .slide{position:static !important;opacity:1 !important;visibility:visible !important;display:block !important;
      width:1040px;min-height:630px;box-sizing:border-box;overflow:visible !important;
      padding:114px 44px 30px !important;page-break-after:always;break-after:page;}
    .slide:last-child{page-break-after:auto;break-after:auto;}
    .slide.inter{display:flex !important;height:auto !important;min-height:576px;}
    .printonly{display:block !important;}

    /* ── lo especifico del modulo 101 ───────────────────────────────────────
       Las slides de video y la del P&ID son cajas flex elasticas: con display
       block sus hijos con flex:1 1 auto y min-height:0 se quedan en cero y no
       imprimen nada. */
    .slide.m101video .vidbox{display:none !important;}      /* un <video> impreso es un rectangulo negro */
    .slide.m101video .vidtabs,.slide.m530pid .pidctl{display:none !important;}
    .slide.m101video .vidfoot{margin-top:14px !important;}
    .pidbox{height:430px !important;min-height:430px !important;overflow:hidden !important;
      border:1px solid var(--line-strong) !important;}
    .pidbox img{position:static !important;transform:none !important;width:100% !important;height:auto !important;}
    .pidhint{display:none !important;}
    .slide.m101ds .eqdetail{height:auto !important;}         /* height:calc(100% - 66px) colapsa sin padre elastico */
    /* el mapa de U530 se queda al ancho de pantalla: al 100% la slide se parte en dos paginas */
    .slide.u530map .mapwrap{max-width:63% !important;}
    /* si una slide desborda igualmente, que el corte caiga ENTRE bloques y no por
       la mitad de un grafico o de una tabla */
    .mapwrap,.carea,.objgrid,.mgrid,.figrow,table,svg,.eqdetail{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid;}
    .slide.u530area .carea{height:330px !important;}
    /* slide 11 (m340cyc) es la misma trampa: caja flex elastica. Con display
       block el .cycfig deja de ser elastico y la imagen con height:100% se
       resolveria a auto y saldria a tamano natural, partiendo la pagina. Se
       fija por altura para que el dibujo y las cuatro tarjetas quepan juntos. */
    .slide.m340cyc,.slide.m340cyc .cycfig{display:block !important;}
    .slide.m340cyc .cycfig img{width:auto !important;height:auto !important;
      max-height:320px !important;max-width:100% !important;}
    .slide.m340cyc .cyccards{break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid;}
  }

  /* ═══ MODULE 103 · additions to the lifted Module-102 stylesheet ═══════════ */

  /* 1 · Cover. Same treatment as Module 102, over the Unit 340 3D capture instead
        of /images/3D_330-bw.png: the render shows the four PK-341 packages top
        right, V-343 and the six E-342 condenser banks. The dark gradient is what
        keeps the white heading legible over the model. Same specificity as
        .slide.cover3d, declared later, therefore it wins. */
  .slide.cover3d.cov340{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(11,13,15,.82),rgba(11,13,15,.55) 45%,rgba(11,13,15,.86)),url('/images/3D_340_bw.png') center/cover no-repeat;}

  /* 1b · .m340cyc — slide 11 only. The manual's R1 sheet is the point of the
        slide, so the figure takes every pixel the stage can spare: the section
        is a flex column, the figure box is the only flexible child, and the img
        is height-driven (width:auto) so it grows until the cards below it stop
        it. No control content lives here — process only. The header and the
        four cards are squeezed to the minimum that still reads at the back of
        the room, because every pixel they give back is a pixel of drawing. */
  .slide.m340cyc{padding:19px 40px 12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden;}
  .slide.m340cyc .kicker{margin-bottom:4px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m340cyc h2{font-size:21px;margin-bottom:6px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cycfig{flex:1 1 auto;min-height:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:4px;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cycfig img{height:100%;width:auto;max-width:100%;object-fit:contain;
    border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:5px;background:#fff;cursor:zoom-in;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cyccards{flex:none;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
    gap:7px;margin-top:8px;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cyccards .step{display:block;align-items:stretch;gap:0;padding:6px 9px;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cyccards .step .u{min-width:0;font-size:10px;margin-bottom:2px;letter-spacing:.03em;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cyccards .step .t{font-size:11.6px;line-height:1.3;}
  .slide.m340cyc .cyccards .step .p{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.2px;line-height:1.3;
    color:var(--crimson);margin-top:3px;letter-spacing:.02em;}

  /* 2 · .eqd340 — the compact one-machine-per-slide layout, the same measurements
        as Module 102's .eqd330: it buys ~55 px so a full-width R1 sheet plus two
        cards still fit the 587 px stage. Scoped to the walkthrough slides only. */
  /* The master PFD is one sheet taller than the per-topic sheets it replaced,
     so the walkthrough slides cap it the way Module 102 caps `amineblock`. */
  .slide.eqd340 .mapwrap .loc svg{max-width:82%;margin:0 auto;}
  .slide.eqd340{padding:23px 44px 13px;}
  .slide.eqd340 h2{margin-bottom:10px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .kicker{margin-bottom:7px;}
  .slide.eqd340 ul.points{margin-top:0;}
  .slide.eqd340 ul.points li{font-size:12.2px;line-height:1.32;padding:3.4px 0 3.4px 18px;}
  .slide.eqd340 ul.points li:before{top:10px;width:6px;height:6px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .ctlwrap,.slide.eqd340 .almwrap{margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .hcard .hh{font-size:8.8px;padding:3.5px 9px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .hcard .hb{padding:4px 9px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .hval{font-size:10.3px;padding:1.3px 0;line-height:1.26;}
  .slide.eqd340 .grid2{gap:10px 20px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .collbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--crimson);font-weight:700;padding:0 0 3px 2px;}
  .slide.eqd340 table.data{font-size:10.4px;line-height:1.2;}
  .slide.eqd340 table.data td{padding:3.2px 7px;}
  .slide.eqd340 table.data th{padding:4px 7px;font-size:8.6px;}

  /* 3 · The R1 sheets are LINE sheets, not box sheets: the lit machine is
        recoloured rather than filled, so the dim level can sit a little higher
        than the global .30 without the highlight losing contrast. */
  .slide.eqd340 .loc[data-hi] [data-eq]{opacity:.34;}
  .slide.eqd340 .loc[data-hi] [data-eq].on{opacity:1;}

  /* 4 · The conflict chip. Every place where two approved documents disagree gets
        one short amber line on the slide itself — never only in the notes. */
  .cr340{margin-top:7px;border-left:3px solid var(--amber);background:#FFF8EC;
    border-radius:0 4px 4px 0;padding:5px 10px;font-size:10.8px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--ink);}
  .cr340 b{color:var(--amber);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.4px;letter-spacing:.06em;
    text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:6px;}
  .slide.eqd340 .cr340{margin-top:6px;font-size:10.2px;padding:4px 9px;}

  /* 4b · .cr340.dgr — the same chip in the DANGER colour. Used only where the
         OEM itself prints a DANGER or WARNING notice (the magnetic coupling
         hazards, the oil-filled-compressor start warning, the emergency stop).
         Amber is for documentation conflicts; crimson is for people. */
  .cr340.dgr{border-left-color:var(--crimson);background:#FBE9EC;}
  .cr340.dgr b{color:var(--crimson);}

  /* 5 · Slide 41 — the cause-and-effect matrix. Module 102's U330 matrix is 8
        causes; Table 7.11 needs 11 rows (5 package causes + the 5 trips it does
        NOT carry + PSD01) plus the provenance legend, and at the global .cematrix
        sizing that is 772 px against a 586 px stage. Tightened HERE only, so the
        U330/U310 matrices this deck does not carry keep their own rhythm. */
  #ce340 table.cematrix{font-size:10.5px;}
  #ce340 table.cematrix th,#ce340 table.cematrix td{padding-top:2.2px;padding-bottom:2.2px;
    line-height:1.24;}
  #ce340 .celegend{font-size:10.3px;line-height:1.42;margin-top:6px;}
  #ce340 .cehint{margin-top:4px;}

  /* 6 · Slide 49 — the document register. 18 rows against Module 102's 15, plus a
        row of drawing buttons. The lifted .m101docs rule was measured on 15. */
  .slide.m101docs table.data{font-size:10.3px !important;}
  .slide.m101docs table.data td,.slide.m101docs table.data th{padding-top:2.4px;
    padding-bottom:2.4px;line-height:1.2;}
  .slide.m101docs .docbtns{margin-bottom:6px;}
  .slide.m101docs .note{margin-top:6px;padding-top:6px;}

  /* 4 · .m103scroll — slides 06 and 07. Both draw their graphic at exactly the
        size Module 102 draws it (no max-height cap), so the stream tags, the
        trunk labels and the GA figure stay legible on a projector. That is
        taller than the 587 px stage, so these slides scroll on purpose:
        .slide already carries
        overflow:auto, and what is added here is only making the scroll VISIBLE --
        a permanent gutter and a styled thumb, plus a caret that fades on first
        scroll so nobody presents the slide without knowing the cards are below.
        The print stylesheet flattens every slide to height:auto, so the export
        is unaffected. */
  /* the 9 px scrollbar gutter is taken off the right padding, so the drawing
     keeps EXACTLY the width it has in Module 102 (930 px on a 1040 px deck) */
  .slide.m103scroll{scrollbar-gutter:stable;scroll-behavior:smooth;padding-right:35px;}
  .slide.m103scroll::-webkit-scrollbar{width:9px;}
  .slide.m103scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-track{background:var(--bg-soft);border-radius:5px;}
  .slide.m103scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:#C9CFD6;border-radius:5px;}
  .slide.m103scroll::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover{background:var(--ink-soft);}
  .slide.m103scroll .scrollcue{position:sticky;bottom:0;display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;
    pointer-events:none;height:0;transition:opacity .3s ease;}
  .slide.m103scroll .scrollcue span{transform:translateY(-14px);font-family:var(--mono);
    font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);
    background:rgba(255,255,255,.92);border:1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius:20px;padding:3px 11px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.08);}
  .slide.m103scroll.scrolled .scrollcue{opacity:0;}
  @media print{.slide.m103scroll .scrollcue{display:none !important;}}

  /* 4b · slide 06 — the area carousel. Module 102's lifted .carousel is 322 px,
        a height measured on HMI captures. Here it carries the Fig. 7.1 general
        arrangement plus four 3D model views of the built unit, so it is given the
        same 430 px the .carea box had: the GA drawing keeps exactly the size it
        had before the carousel existed, and the wide 3D views (about 2.2:1)
        become height-limited rather than width-limited. No captions -- the
        pictures carry their own tags (E-342, PK-341-1) and what to say about
        each view is in the presenter notes. Scoped to this slide only. */
  .slide.u530area .carousel{height:430px;margin-top:2px;}
  .slide.u530area .carousel .cimg img{max-height:414px;}
  .slide.u530area .carousel .cdots{bottom:-13px;}
  /* on paper a carousel would print ONE frame and silently drop the other four.
     The print stylesheet already flattens .slide to height:auto, so the frames
     are simply unstacked and all five come out in order. */
  @media print{
    .slide.u530area .carousel{height:auto;}
    .slide.u530area .carousel .cimg{position:static;opacity:1;pointer-events:auto;
      page-break-inside:avoid;margin-bottom:12px;}
    .slide.u530area .carousel .cimg img{max-height:none;width:100%;}
    .slide.u530area .carousel .cdots{display:none;}
  }

  /* 5 · .m103disc — slide 06 only. The four discipline squares arrive from
        tam-disc as one <svg> each: a header band (title + total, 32 of the 210
        viewBox units) and, under it, the treemap of asset classes. On this deck
        the slide has to open on the ARRANGEMENT, so the mosaic is folded away
        and only the totals show; the presenter opens the ones the room asks
        about. The header here is real HTML, not the svg one -- and because it
        repeats what the svg already draws, the svg is pulled up by exactly
        32/210 = 15.24 % of its own width so its band is cropped, never printed
        twice. Percentage, not pixels, so it holds at any column width. */
  .slide.m103disc .dband{align-items:start;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsq{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:9px;
    background:#fff;overflow:hidden;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd{width:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;
    justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;padding:8px 11px;background:var(--bg-soft);
    border:0;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;cursor:pointer;text-align:left;
    font-family:var(--mono);transition:background .15s ease;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd:hover{background:#fff;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsq.open .dsqhd{border-bottom-color:var(--line);}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .t{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;min-width:0;
    font-size:8.4px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--ink-soft);
    overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .chip{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:3px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .c{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:5px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .n{font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);line-height:1;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .u{font-size:6.6px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;
    color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .chev{font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1;
    transition:transform .22s ease;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsq.open .dsqhd .chev{transform:rotate(180deg);}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqbody{overflow:hidden;max-height:0;transition:max-height .3s ease;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsq.open .dsqbody{max-height:620px;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqbody svg{margin-top:-15.24%;}
  .slide.m103disc .dsqfoot{margin:0;padding:4px 9px 7px;}
  /* the export is not interactive, so it prints every square open */
  @media print{
    .slide.m103disc .dsqbody{max-height:none !important;}
    .slide.m103disc .dsqhd .chev{display:none !important;}
  }

  /* 6 · .m103safe — slides 08, 09, 10, the ammonia safety cluster. These three
        used to be four dense bullet lists; a safety slide read off the screen
        is a safety slide nobody remembers. The prose moved into data-notes,
        where the presenter has it, and the screen keeps blocks: pictograms,
        short labelled cards, a dose ladder, numbered steps and one red line.
        Symbols are drawn inline by tools/safety_icons.py — schematic GHS and
        ISO 7010, never plant signage. */
  .slide.m103safe .symrow{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.m103safe .ghs,.slide.m103safe .sgn{flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:3px;border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:8px;padding:5px 3px 4px;background:var(--bg-soft);}
  .slide.m103safe .ghs svg,.slide.m103safe .sgn svg{width:34px;height:34px;display:block;}
  .slide.m103safe .sgn svg{width:31px;height:31px;}
  .slide.m103safe .symrow.big{gap:10px;margin-top:9px;}
  .slide.m103safe .symrow.big .ghs{padding:9px 4px 7px;gap:5px;}
  .slide.m103safe .symrow.big .ghs svg{width:58px;height:58px;}
  .slide.m103safe .symrow.big .ghs b{font-size:8px;}
  .slide.m103safe .ghs b,.slide.m103safe .sgn b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:6.8px;
    font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);
    text-align:center;line-height:1.25;}

  /* the block card: a colour-keyed strip and at most four short lines under it */
  .slide.m103safe .blks{display:grid;gap:8px;margin-top:8px;}
  .slide.m103safe .blks.c2{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}
  .slide.m103safe .blks.c3{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);}
  .slide.m103safe .blks.c4{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);}
  .slide.m103safe .blk{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;
    background:#fff;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk > b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.09em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:#fff;background:var(--ink);padding:4px 9px;
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk > b svg{width:14px;height:14px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk.red > b{background:var(--crimson);}
  .slide.m103safe .blk.amb > b{background:#B07B00;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk.grn > b{background:#2E7D46;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk.blu > b{background:#0B5FA5;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk ul{margin:0;padding:5px 9px 6px;list-style:none;}
  .slide.m103safe .blk li{font-size:10.6px;line-height:1.34;padding:2px 0 2px 11px;
    position:relative;color:var(--ink);}
  .slide.m103safe .blk li:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:8px;width:5px;
    height:5px;border-radius:1.5px;background:var(--line-strong);}
  .slide.m103safe .blk li b{font-family:var(--mono);}
  .slide.m103safe .blk .big{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:15px;font-weight:700;
    padding:5px 9px 0;line-height:1;}

  /* the one red line per slide — the sentence that is not negotiable */
  .slide.m103safe .redline{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;margin-top:8px;
    border:1.6px solid var(--crimson);border-radius:8px;background:#FDECEF;padding:6px 12px;}
  .slide.m103safe .redline svg{width:30px;height:30px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103safe .redline span{font-size:12.4px;font-weight:700;color:#8A0B20;line-height:1.3;}
  .slide.m103safe .redline i{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.6px;
    font-weight:400;color:var(--ink-soft);display:block;margin-top:1px;}

  /* dose ladder — three steps, colour is the severity */
  .slide.m103safe .dose{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px;margin-top:8px;}
  .slide.m103safe .dose div{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;
    padding:6px 10px 7px;background:#fff;border-top:4px solid;}
  .slide.m103safe .dose .lo{border-top-color:#E8B54B;}
  .slide.m103safe .dose .md{border-top-color:#E2701E;}
  .slide.m103safe .dose .hi{border-top-color:var(--crimson);}
  .slide.m103safe .dose em{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:7.6px;
    font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-soft);}
  .slide.m103safe .dose p{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:10.8px;line-height:1.3;}

  /* numbered response steps */
  .slide.m103safe .steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:8px;margin-top:8px;}
  .slide.m103safe .steps div{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;
    background:var(--bg-soft);padding:6px 9px 7px;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;}
  .slide.m103safe .steps u{text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;
    font-weight:700;color:var(--crimson);line-height:1;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103safe .steps p{margin:0;font-size:10.6px;line-height:1.3;}
  .slide.m103safe .steps p b{font-family:var(--mono);}

  /* the NEVER strip — prohibition signs with their one-line reason */
  .slide.m103safe .never{display:flex;gap:10px;margin-top:8px;align-items:stretch;}
  .slide.m103safe .never > div{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;
    border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;background:#fff;padding:5px 10px;}
  .slide.m103safe .never svg{width:26px;height:26px;flex:none;}
  .slide.m103safe .never span{font-size:10.4px;line-height:1.28;}
  .slide.m103safe .never span b{font-family:var(--mono);}

  /* H-codes as chips, not as a paragraph */
  .slide.m103safe .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px;margin-top:7px;}
  .slide.m103safe .chip{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:5px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius:20px;background:#fff;padding:2.5px 10px;font-size:10.2px;line-height:1.25;}
  .slide.m103safe .chip b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.4px;color:var(--crimson);}
  .slide.m103safe .facts{margin-top:4px;}
  .slide.m103safe table.data{font-size:10.4px;line-height:1.18;}
  .slide.m103safe table.data td,.slide.m103safe table.data th{padding:2.6px 7px;}

</style>
</head>
<body>
<svg id="symlib340" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden"><defs><marker id="aD1410C" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#D1410C"/></marker><marker id="a1F8A4C" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#1F8A4C"/></marker><marker id="a0B5CAD" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#0B5CAD"/></marker><marker id="a00A0B0" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#00A0B0"/></marker><marker id="aB26A00" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#B26A00"/></marker><marker id="a8B939C" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#8B939C"/></marker><marker id="a7A5C00" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="5.5" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6.5,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#7A5C00"/></marker></defs></svg>
<div class="deck">

  <header class="brandbar">
    <div class="vendor"><img src="/images/logoTA.png" alt="Technical America" /></div>
    <div class="clients">
      <span class="role">Clients</span>
      <div class="client-logos">
        <img class="client-logo" src="/images/logoME.png" alt="Manaenergy" />
        <span class="divider"></span>
        <img class="client-logo itf" src="/images/logoITF.png" alt="ITF — Italfluid" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="accent"></div>

  <div class="stage" id="stage">

<section class="slide cover3d cov340" data-min="2" data-block="Module open" data-presenter="" data-notes='["Welcome to Module 103 &#8212; Unit 340, the ammonia refrigeration loop, the utility that both Unit 310 and Unit 350 depend on.", "Everything today comes from the Plant Operating Manual 21044-PR-MAN-00001 section 7, the UFD PRO10-ING-PR07 and the five P&amp;IDs PR34 to PR38, cross-checked against the plant database.", "Set the frame in one sentence: this is a closed loop that never mixes with the gas &#8212; the same ammonia goes round and round, and its only job is to move heat out of two exchangers.", "Say the safety line early and mean it: ammonia is toxic and corrosive, and any loss of containment in this unit is a significant hazard. We come back to that on slides 08–10 and again on slide 43.", "Same four-hour format as the previous modules: breaks at 2:00 and at 3:15, exam and evaluation at the end."]'><div class="kicker">Module 103 &#183; Operation <span class="sub">&#8212; 18-module program</span></div><h1>Unit 340 &#8212;<br>Ammonia Refrigeration</h1><p class="lead">Tendrara Micro LNG Facilities &#8212; operator training program. The closed R1 ammonia loop designed to EN 378: four screw-compressor trains, six air-cooled condensers, one receiver, two evaporators.</p><div class="facts params"><div class="fact"><div class="n">PK-341-1&#8230;4</div><div class="l">four screw trains &#183; 3 working + 1 standby &#183; selected by hand</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">28 barg</div><div class="l">loop design pressure &#183; PSV-3401A/B on V-343 set here</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">E-311 &#183; E-354</div><div class="l">the two evaporators the whole unit exists to feed</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">XAHH-3401</div><div class="l">ammonia gas detection 2ooN &#8594; PSD</div></div></div><div class="owner">Client: <b>ManaEnergy</b> &#183; Source: <b>21044-PR-MAN-00001 &#183; &#167;7</b> &#183; P&amp;IDs <b>PR34&#8211;PR38</b></div></section>
<section class="slide" data-min="2" data-block="Module open" data-presenter="" data-notes='["18 four-hour modules, live online, 08 Jul to 17 Aug 2026.", "Two Fundamentals modules plus sixteen Operation modules unit by unit &#8212; Module 103 is the third unit module.", "Every module follows the same shape: objectives, content, questions, exam and evaluation. Safety first, technician focused.", "Remind the group where 103 sits: straight after the gas treatment pair, and immediately before the two liquefaction modules that consume most of this cooling."]'><div class="kicker">Welcome &#183; The program</div><h2>About this training program</h2><p class="lead">A technical program for LNG plant personnel, built around the <b>Tendrara Micro LNG</b> facility &#8212; from gas fundamentals to unit-by-unit operation and the control room.</p><div class="facts" style="margin-top:6px;"><div class="fact"><div class="n">18</div><div class="l">modules total</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">4 h</div><div class="l">per module &#183; live online</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">~72 h</div><div class="l">total training</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="n">Jul&#8211;Aug</div><div class="l">2026 delivery window</div></div></div><ul class="points" style="margin-top:12px;"><li><b>2 Fundamentals</b> modules + <b>16 Operation</b> modules (unit-by-unit &amp; control room).</li><li>Each module: <b>objectives &#8594; content &#8594; Q&amp;A &#8594; exam &amp; evaluation.</b> <b>Safety-first, technician-focused.</b></li></ul></section>
<section class="slide" data-min="2" data-block="Module open" data-presenter="" data-notes='["Each instructor introduces himself &#8212; about one minute each.", "1 &#183; BILL GARCIA &#8212; CEO, Technical America: company overview and commitment to the training program [complete with your background and years].", "2 &#183; JIMMY BIONDI &#8212; PhD Engineer: process and refrigeration engineering expertise [complete].", "3 &#183; MARIO MENDIZABAL &#8212; Control &amp; Systems Manager: plant data model, documentation and training system for the Tendrara facility [complete].", "Common closing: Technical America is the technology vendor and the training provider; questions are welcome at any slide, and the exam only covers what we present."]'><div class="kicker">Your instructors</div><h2>Meet the team</h2><div class="team"><div class="person"><div class="av">BG</div><div class="nm">Bill Garcia</div><div class="rl">CEO &#8212; Technical America</div></div><div class="person"><div class="av zr">JB</div><div class="nm">Jimmy Biondi</div><div class="rl zr">Process Engineer (PhD)</div></div><div class="person"><div class="av gn">MM</div><div class="nm">Mario Mendizabal</div><div class="rl gn">Control &amp; Systems Manager</div></div></div><div class="note">Technical America &#8212; technology vendor &amp; training provider. Who presents which block is left open on purpose &#8212; the agenda names the blocks, not the speakers.</div></section>
<section class="slide" data-min="2" data-block="Module open" data-presenter="" data-notes='["18 modules: 2 Fundamentals plus 16 Operation, 08 Jul to 17 Aug 2026.", "Today is Module 103 &#8212; ONE unit for the first time, and a utility rather than a process unit: Unit 340 serves other units, it does not touch the product gas.", "Point forward: modules 104 and 105 are liquefaction, and E-354 &#8212; the biggest consumer of this loop &#8212; belongs to them. What we cool here is what makes the cold box possible.", "Each Operation module keeps the same skeleton: principle of operation, main components, control loops, valves, alarms and daily checks."]'><div class="kicker">Roadmap &#183; 18 modules &#183; 4 h each</div><h2>Program roadmap</h2><div class="grid2" style="gap:10px 22px;"><table class="data" style="font-size:12px;"><tr><th colspan="2" style="color:var(--crimson);">Fundamentals</th></tr><tr><td class="k">001</td><td>Intro to LNG &amp; Tendrara facility</td></tr><tr><td class="k">002</td><td>Facility operation, safety &amp; emergency</td></tr><tr><th colspan="2" style="color:var(--crimson);">Operation &#8212; unit by unit</th></tr><tr><td class="k">101</td><td>U200 Inlet &amp; U530 Process Water Treatment</td></tr><tr><td class="k">102</td><td>U330/310 Sweetening &amp; Dehydration</td></tr><tr style="background:#FBE9EC;"><td class="k" style="color:var(--crimson);">103 &#9656;</td><td><b>U340 Refrigeration</b> <span class="muted">(today)</span></td></tr><tr><td class="k">104</td><td>U350 Liquefaction I</td></tr><tr><td class="k">105</td><td>U350 Liquefaction II</td></tr><tr><td class="k">106</td><td>U360 Flash/BOG &amp; U370 NGL Vaporizer</td></tr><tr><td class="k">107</td><td>U220 Storage &amp; Dispensing</td></tr></table><table class="data" style="font-size:12px;"><tr><th colspan="2" style="color:var(--crimson);">Operation (cont.)</th></tr><tr><td class="k">108</td><td>U500/600 Air &amp; N&#8322; + U540 Water</td></tr><tr><td class="k">109</td><td>U410 Hot oil</td></tr><tr><td class="k">110</td><td>U430 Analyzers</td></tr><tr><td class="k">111</td><td>U480/490 Power Gen I</td></tr><tr><td class="k">112</td><td>U480/490 Power Gen II</td></tr><tr><td class="k">113</td><td>U230/700/550/730 Flare, F&amp;G, Drain, Fire</td></tr><tr><td class="k">114</td><td>Control Room / Console I (PCS, HMI)</td></tr><tr><td class="k">115</td><td>Control Room / Console II</td></tr><tr><td class="k">116</td><td>Plant start-stop &amp; LNG truck loading</td></tr></table></div></section>
<section class="slide m101scope" data-min="4" data-block="Module open" data-presenter="" data-notes='["Read the objectives out loud &#8212; they are the exam blueprint, and nothing outside them is examined.", "Four blocks, and the order is deliberate. Block 1 is the unit and the fluid &#8212; where it sits and why ammonia has to be respected before we open a single valve. Block 2 walks the process once round the closed loop without stopping: suction, discharge, condensers, receiver, distribution, the two users, and back. Block 3 then opens the one item we deliberately left as a black box &#8212; the PK-341 compressor package &#8212; and takes it apart down to the complete lubrication system. Block 4 is control, protection, operation and maintenance.", "Tell the room explicitly on the suction slide that we are stepping past the compressor for now and will open it after the loop is closed &#8212; otherwise they will think we skipped it.", "Say what is new in this revision: the vendor package manual for PK-341 is now folded in, so the compressor, the slide valve, the oil separator internals, the pump, the cooler, the filters and the whole maintenance schedule are covered at vendor level of detail.", "Warn the room once, here: this unit has real documentation conflicts &#8212; fan counts, motor ratings, valve tags, and now three different slide-valve ranges and three different coalescer thresholds. We show them as they are and mark them as open points rather than choosing quietly.", "The four-hour skeleton is on the right. Breaks start at 2:05 and at 3:15; the per-slide minute sums in the deck are the only real timetable, and they agree with this table."]'><div class="kicker">Scope &#183; Objectives &#183; Agenda</div><h2>What Module 103 covers</h2><div class="grid2"><div><p class="lead" style="margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);">Objectives &#8212; by the end you can:</p><ul class="points"><li><b>Purpose</b> &#8212; why the loop exists and the two exchangers it feeds (<b>E-311</b>, <b>E-354</b>).</li><li><b>Ammonia safety</b> &#8212; exposure limits (20 ppm / 8 h, 50 ppm / 15 min), PPE, first aid, leak response.</li><li><b>R1 cycle</b> &#8212; compress &#8594; condense &#8594; collect &#8594; expand &amp; evaporate &#8594; suction, and the pressure ladder 28 &#8594; 20 barg.</li><li><b>Around the loop</b> &#8212; E-342-1&#8230;6, V-343, liquid distribution, E-311 / E-354, hot gas and relief.</li><li><b>PK-341 package</b> &#8212; C/V/P/E/F/X-341 item by item.</li><li><b>Screw compressor</b> &#8212; slide valve, oil injection, and the lube system (<b>PDI-3414.1 &gt; 1.5 bar D</b>).</li><li><b>Control &amp; protection</b> &#8212; loops, interlocks, critical trips incl. <b>XAHH-3401</b> 2ooN &#8594; PSD.</li><li><b>Maintenance</b> &#8212; the daily-to-annual round, filter/coalescer thresholds, oil, overhaul hours.</li></ul></div><div><table class="timeline"><tr><td class="seg"><b>Module open</b><span class="tp">program &#183; team &#183; roadmap &#183; scope</span></td><td class="dur">0:12</td><td class="cum">0:12</td></tr><tr><td class="seg"><b>Block 1 &#8212; the unit and the fluid</b><span class="tp">the area &#183; interfaces &#183; ammonia hazard, safety data sheet, first aid &amp; PPE</span></td><td class="dur">0:19</td><td class="cum">0:31</td></tr><tr><td class="seg"><b>Block 2 &#8212; the process, once round the loop</b><span class="tp">principle &#183; R1 cycle &#183; the numbers &#183; suction &#183; discharge &#183; condensers &#183; receiver &#183; distribution &#183; the two users &#183; hot gas &#183; relief</span></td><td class="dur">0:40</td><td class="cum">1:11</td></tr><tr><td class="seg"><b>Block 3 &#8212; the compressor package &amp; lubrication</b><span class="tp">four trains &#183; screw compressor &#183; slide valve &#183; separator &amp; coalescers &#183; lube-oil circuits &#183; pump &#183; magnetic coupling &#183; cooler &#183; filters &#183; oil &#916;P &#183; housekeeping</span></td><td class="dur">0:39</td><td class="cum">1:50</td></tr><tr class="brk"><td class="seg">&#9749; Break</td><td class="dur">0:15</td><td class="cum">2:05</td></tr><tr><td class="seg"><b>Block 4 &#8212; control, protection &amp; maintenance</b><span class="tp">valves &#183; instruments &#183; loops &#183; HMI &#183; C&amp;E &#183; interlocks &#183; gas detection &#183; start/stop &#183; monitoring &#183; overhaul &#183; troubleshooting</span></td><td class="dur">0:55</td><td class="cum">3:00</td></tr><tr class="brk"><td class="seg">&#9749; Break</td><td class="dur">0:15</td><td class="cum">3:15</td></tr><tr><td class="seg">Questions &amp; answers</td><td class="dur">0:15</td><td class="cum">3:30</td></tr><tr><td class="seg">Exam + module evaluation</td><td class="dur">0:30</td><td class="cum">4:00</td></tr><tr class="tot"><td class="seg">Module total</td><td class="dur">4:00</td><td class="cum"></td></tr></table></div></div></section>
<section class="slide u530area m103scroll m103disc" data-min="4" data-block="Block 1" data-presenter="" data-notes='["Open Block 1 physically. Five views rotate here, and it is worth clicking through them by hand rather than letting them cycle. The first is Manual Fig. 7.1, the general arrangement with the risk locations marked &#8212; the shower and spillage kit at E-342-4, the extinguishers at E-342-1 and PK-341-1. The other four are the 3D model of the unit as built.", "Use the model to fix the layout in the room before any P&amp;ID appears: six E-342 condenser banks in one line on green portal steel, four PK-341 skids on a single plinth facing them, each skid carrying its own E-341 oil cooler, and the receiver group at the end. Tags are legible in views 4 and 5 &#8212; point at PK-341-1 and at E-342-1 on the picture and everyone has a place to hang the rest of the afternoon on.", "Size of the system: 476 registry assets. 89 mechanical, 120 electrical, 151 instrumentation, 111 control, plus 5 fire-equipment items. The four squares open on the totals only &#8212; click a header to unfold the mosaic of asset classes inside that discipline, and then any tile in it to print the underlying records.", "The mechanical square is dominated by fans: 73 of the 89 mechanical assets are fans, because every condenser and oil-cooler fan is its own asset. That is what a refrigeration unit looks like in a register.", "Two honesty points that will come back all afternoon. First, ZERO manual valves are digitised for Unit 340 &#8212; do not quote a valve line-up count from this deck. Second, only train 1 is digitised at equipment level, so a four-identical-trains picture is built by inference, not read from the register.", "Note also that the five gas detectors GD-05 to GD-09 live in the safety-device table only; they are not registry assets, so they do not appear in these squares."]'><div class="kicker">Unit 340 &#183; The area physically <span class="sub">&#8212; location &#183; size &#183; technological objects</span></div><h2>Where it sits, how big it is, what is inside</h2><div class="mapwrap" style="padding:7px 10px 12px;"><div class="lbl"><span>Unit 340 &#8212; the area in five views: the GA drawing, then the 3D model</span><span class="you">&#9632; compressor shelter &#183; condenser bank &#183; receiver</span></div><div class="carousel" id="area340" data-interval="6500"><a class="cimg active" href="/images/unit340-GA-risk.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/unit340-GA-risk.png" alt="Unit 340 general arrangement and risk locations, Manual Fig. 7.1"></a><a class="cimg" href="/images/3D_340_01.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/3D_340_01.png" alt="Unit 340 3D model, elevated view over the condenser bank and the four packages"></a><a class="cimg" href="/images/3D_340_02.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/3D_340_02.png" alt="Unit 340 3D model, the condenser row seen along its length with the packages behind"></a><a class="cimg" href="/images/3D_340_03.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/3D_340_03.png" alt="Unit 340 3D model, the four PK-341 packages with E-342-1 and E-342-2 tagged behind"></a><a class="cimg" href="/images/3D_340_04.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/3D_340_04.png" alt="Unit 340 3D model, close view of the PK-341 skid line and the E-342 bank"></a><div class="cdots"><b class="active"></b><b></b><b></b><b></b><b></b></div></div></div><div class="dband" id="objtiles340"></div><div class="objmodal" id="objmodal340"><div class="objbox"><div class="objhd"><span id="objtitle340">&#8212;</span><button id="objclose340" aria-label="close">&#10005;</button></div><div class="objtblwrap" id="objwrap340"></div><div class="objfoot">Source: Tendrara plant database (local copy) &#183; Unit 340 &#183; read 3 Aug 2026 &#183; MECH 89 &#183; ELEC 120 &#183; INST 151 &#183; CTRL 111 &#183; fire equipment 5</div></div></div><div class="scrollcue"><span>&#9662; scroll for the squares</span></div></section>
<section class="slide m103scroll" data-min="4" data-block="Block 1" data-presenter="" data-notes='["Same plant map the trainees saw in Module 102, re-pointed: Unit 340 is the crimson box at the top now. Show them where they are before you show them what crosses the fence &#8212; and note that this unit sits OFF the main gas line, not on it.", "Only four fluids cross the fence. Liquid ammonia out to the two users, hot gas out to the same two users, ammonia vapour back from both, and relief out to the ammonia flare header. Nothing else &#8212; the refrigerant never mixes with the process gas, which is why the cyan AMMONIA (R717) trunk on the map only touches U310 and U350.", "The size of the service is the left card, and it is the number to carry all afternoon: 4 751 kW of refrigeration, of which E-354 in Unit 350 takes 4 318 kW &#8212; about ninety per cent. Unit 340 exists for liquefaction; E-311 is the small consumer.", "The six tie-ins by line number, if the room asks: liquid to E-311 is 1&#189;-inch AN-000201 and its hot gas AN-000208; liquid to E-354 is 4-inch AN-000124 and its hot gas 3-inch AN-000125; the vapour comes back on 3-inch AN-000204-C25 and 10-inch AN-000123-C35. Relief is 3-inch FL-000026 to Unit 230 and the charging point is 354-HV-201. All six were checked against PR08 and PR22 and all six match.", "One signal also crosses the fence and it matters: PIC-3552 from Unit 350 arrives at all four compressor packages and sets their capacity through the slide valves. The unit is loaded from outside &#8212; nobody in Unit 340 decides how hard it works.", "If anyone challenges the 4 751 kW against the 560 kW on the compressor slide: 4 751 is the sum of the two user duties in the HMB (433 + 4 318), while 560 kW is the MC-341-x MOTOR rating, which the vendor data block mislabels as cooling duty. Three motors of 560 kW cannot make 4 751 kW of cold. The change request is open and it is listed on the open-points slide."]'><div class="kicker">Unit 340 &#183; Area