chor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">800 mm ID &#183; 5000 mm TL-TL &#183; 2.5 m&#179; &#183; LTCS &#183; FV/28 barg &#183; &#8722;45/120 &#176;C</text><text x="333" y="270" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">LLL 180 mm from the bottom tangent line</text><g transform="translate(224,180)"><title>PT-3401 &#183; 0..28 barg &#183; PAH 27 / PAL 20</title><circle cx="0" cy="0" r="11" fill="#fff" stroke="#15171A" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="0" y="-2.2" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="7.4" font-weight="700" fill="#15171A">PT</text><text x="0" y="6.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.6" font-weight="400" fill="#15171A">3401</text></g><path d="M 224,191 L 224,204" fill="none" stroke="#8B939C" stroke-width="1.1"/><g transform="translate(286,180)"><title>LT-3401 &#183; V-343 level &#183; LAL 25 %</title><circle cx="0" cy="0" r="11" fill="#fff" stroke="#15171A" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="0" y="-2.2" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="7.4" font-weight="700" fill="#15171A">LT</text><text x="0" y="6.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.6" font-weight="400" fill="#15171A">3401</text></g><path d="M 286,191 L 286,204" fill="none" stroke="#8B939C" stroke-width="1.1"/><text x="224" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">pressure</text><text x="286" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">level</text><text x="360" y="180" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">SG-3401A/B sight glasses &#183; PG-3402 local gauge</text><text x="360" y="189" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">drain D1 2&quot; on 340-HV-026</text><g transform="translate(560,196)"><title>PIC-3401 &#183; the only registered controller in the unit</title><rect x="-11" y="-11" width="22" height="22" fill="#fff" stroke="#15171A" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="0" cy="0" r="10.6" fill="none" stroke="#15171A" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="-11" y1="0" x2="11" y2="0" stroke="#15171A" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="0" y="-2.2" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="7.4" font-weight="700" fill="#15171A">PIC</text><text x="0" y="6.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.6" font-weight="400" fill="#15171A">3401</text></g><path d="M 238,196 L 548,196" fill="none" stroke="#4A4F57" stroke-width="1.15" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><g transform="translate(393.0,196)"><circle cx="-4" cy="0" r="1.9" fill="#fff" stroke="#4A4F57" stroke-width="1.15"/><circle cx="4" cy="0" r="1.9" fill="#fff" stroke="#4A4F57" stroke-width="1.15"/></g><path d="M-4.5,-3 L1,0 L-4.5,3 Z" fill="#4A4F57" transform="translate(548,196)"/><text x="560" y="228" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="7" font-weight="700" fill="#C8102E">PIC-3401</text><text x="560" y="238" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#4A4F57">0..28 barg &#183; SP 25 barg</text><path d="M 574,196 L 730,196 L 730,45 L 838,45" fill="none" stroke="#8B939C" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-dasharray="5 3"/><text x="844" y="47" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">to the fan motors of all six condensers</text><text x="716" y="193" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.8" font-weight="700" fill="#C8102E">RECEIVER PRESSURE STARTS AND STOPS THE FANS</text><text x="716" y="204" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.4" fill="#4A4F57">pressure rising &#8594; more fans on &#183; falling &#8594; fans off, in a set order</text><text x="716" y="214" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.4" fill="#8B939C">on/off with hysteresis &#8212; it is NOT a modulating loop, and it is why the</text><text x="716" y="224" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.4" fill="#8B939C">fan count on the screen changes by itself all day</text><text x="716" y="238" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.4" font-weight="700" fill="#4A4F57">too high &#8594; compressor power and trips &#183; too low &#8594; the users lose liquid</text><line x1="14" y1="272" x2="986" y2="272" stroke="#D6DAE0" stroke-width=".8"/><text x="14" y="284" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.4" fill="#4A4F57">The receiver is the BUFFER: it holds the refrigerant inventory and separates the condensing side from the evaporating side, so the two can run at different rates.</text><text x="986" y="284" text-anchor="end" font-family="Consolas,monospace" font-size="6.2" fill="#8B939C">PRO13-ING-PR38 rev 8</text></svg>',
